</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Analysis of Scaling pQuant</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main results in <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.1 Experimental setup ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ pQuant: Towards Effective Low-Bit Language Models via Decoupled Linear Quantization-Aware Training" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 2</span></a> suggests that merely increasing the parameter count is insufficient for extracting additional information in the extremely low-bit scenario. The expressive capacity of 1-bit tensor is highly constrained under the absmean quantization scheme, limiting its scalability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The <a href="#A4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix D Analysis of Scaling pQuant ‣ pQuant: Towards Effective Low-Bit Language Models via Decoupled Linear Quantization-Aware Training" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 5</span></a> below presents the complete performance test results after scaling.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T5" class="ltx_table">
