<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Overhead of Model Parameter</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although the number of activated parameters during inference in pQuant is consistent with that of other models, the overall parameter count increases with varying N values. Specifically, the total parameter counts for models of different sizes, when N is 1, 2, 4 or 8 are shown in the <a href="#A4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ D.1 Overhead of Model Parameter ‣ Appendix D Analysis of Scaling pQuant ‣ pQuant: Towards Effective Low-Bit Language Models via Decoupled Linear Quantization-Aware Training" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 6</span></a>. When N=1, pQuant has the same number of parameters as normal transformers model.</p>
</div>
